# Line endings are part of this repo's integrity claim, not a local preference.
#
# Default: normalise text to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored upstream suite is hashed byte-for-byte in
# tests/original/MANIFEST.json, and tools/extract/lib/hashes.js deliberately does
# not normalise line endings — a CRLF conversion is exactly the silent edit the
# manifest exists to catch.
#
# Without this rule, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# line ending on checkout, so a fresh clone on Windows fails `make verify-original`
# on all 47 files while nothing has actually been modified. Pin the bytes.
tests/original/** -text

# The recorded fixtures back the parity claim and are quoted by byte size; keep
# them byte-identical across platforms for the same reason.
testdata/original/** -text

# testdata/emit is regenerated and `git diff --exit-code`d in CI on ubuntu while
# being generated on Windows here, so a line-ending rewrite on either side reads
# as generator drift. Pin the bytes, same as above.
testdata/emit/** -text
